15 0 obj
<< /A 44 0 R /Alt (Kaplan-Meier survival plot shows percent survival over four hundred days of treatment under different pH conditions, with a schematic below detailing experimental design for control, short-term, and long-term ocean acidification exposures at pH eight point zero, seven point eight, and seven point five. Survival is lower in the pH seven point five group, especially long term, with annotated arrows indicating RNA-Seq sampling points and accelerated mortality at the lowest pH.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 30 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 45 0 R /Alt (Principal component analysis \(PCA\) plot displays data points for five treatment groups, each with unique color-coded shapes and elliptical confidence intervals. Accompanying heatmaps illustrate associated gene expression pathways, with a Z-score legend from blue to red. Treatment groups are labeled and correspond to distinct clusters.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 32 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 46 0 R /Alt (Two volcano plots display differential gene expression in organisms acclimated for eight hours to pH 7.8 \(top\) and pH 7.5 \(bottom\). Plots show log2 fold change versus negative log10 P values; highlighted gene names indicate some with significant expression changes. Accompanying shaded boxes summarize the number of differentially expressed genes \(DEGs\), significant enriched biological processes for lower and higher expression in ocean acidification conditions, and the count of shared DEGs between treatments. Color-coded gene names and process functions are provided for each condition.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 33 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 47 0 R /Alt (Volcano plot displaying differentially expressed genes among OA treatments at day eighty-eight, with dots representing genes. Upregulated genes in red \(right, log two fold change > zero\), downregulated genes in blue \(left, log two fold change < zero\), and non-significant genes in gray. Key gene names are labeled, including ACAT2, OtopLc, HSP71, and Ddx17. Shaded blue and red regions highlight significant genes. Text box on the right summarizes gene functions by category: stress response, chitin catabolism, acid-base balance, and genome maintenance, with red headings and gene names in black.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 34 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 48 0 R /Alt (Nine grouped box plots display normalized gene expression values for nine genes under five experimental conditions: control \(green\), moderate OA 8-hour \(yellow\), severe OA 8-hour \(orange\), moderate OA 88-day \(light yellow\), and severe OA 88-day \(red\). Each plot highlights differences among the treatments for each gene: HSP90AA1, CUPA3_2, MUCB1, SLC15A1, MRPL30, MOIH_3, Cad87A, NUP43, Pnlip_1, OtopLc, Il\(2\)dtl, and CA7. Data are shown as individual distributions with boxes, whiskers, and outliers for each condition, facilitating comparison of expression changes across treatments.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 36 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
